* DATA supplies the ACCOUNT constructor and the assignable BAL field selector.
* GT(N,0) succeeds for positive amounts. :F(DONE) skips the update on zero or a negative amount.
* Assigning BAL(A) to DEPOSIT makes the current balance the return value on either path.
    DATA('ACCOUNT(BAL)')
    DEFINE('DEPOSIT(A,N)')
    A = ACCOUNT(5)
    OUTPUT = DEPOSIT(A,2) :(END)
DEPOSIT GT(N,0) :F(DONE)
    BAL(A) = BAL(A) + N
DONE DEPOSIT = BAL(A) :(RETURN)
END
